# =============================================================================
# Yogya Mobile — Environment Configuration Example
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env` or `.env.local` to connect to your local backend.
# In Expo SDK 49+, variables prefixed with `EXPO_PUBLIC_` are safely made
# available client-side via `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_*`.
#
# IMPORTANT NETWORK RULES FOR MOBILE TESTING:
# 1. Physical Device (Expo Go over Wi-Fi):
#    - Do NOT use "http://localhost:8000" or "http://127.0.0.1:8000".
#      On a phone, "localhost" refers to the phone itself, NOT your PC!
#    - Use your PC's local Wi-Fi / LAN IP, e.g.:
#      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.15:8000
#
# 2. Android Emulator:
#    - Android emulator aliases your host machine's loopback to 10.0.2.2:
#      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000
#
# 3. Remote Staging / Tunnel (e.g. ngrok / Cloudflare Tunnel / Railway):
#    - EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-tunnel-subdomain.ngrok-free.app
#
# 4. Fallback Demonstration Mode:
#    - Leave EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL blank to run in offline / mock demonstration mode.
# =============================================================================

EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
